==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|rarified}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Distant from the lives and everyday concerns of ordinary people; [[esoteric|esoteric]], [[exclusive]], [[select]].
#: {{ux|en|Philosophical debates can be quite '''rarefied'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Eliot Middlemarch|book=IV|chapter=XXXIV|passage=The country gentry of old time lived in a '''rarefied''' social air: dotted apart on their stations up the mountain they looked down with imperfect discrimination on the belts of thicker life below.}}
#* {{RQ:Doyle Lost World|chapter=II|passage=Of course, Beaumont was the real boss; but he lived in the '''rarefied''' atmosphere of some Olympian height from which he could distinguish nothing smaller than an international crisis or a split in the Cabinet.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|work=FT Weekend|date=2023-04-29|title=Inside the world of the elite nanny|author=Lou Stoppard|passage=One day, she had to present the children, dressing them formally and introducing them by their full titles, ahead of high tea with extended family. It had been a crash course into the '''rarefied''' world in which some Norland charges live.}}
# Elevated in style or nature, [[sublime]]; of high intellectual or moral value.
# {{lb|en|of a gas etc.}} Less [[dense]] than usual; [[thin]].
#: {{ux|en|The air at high altitudes at the top of mountains is '''rarefied'''.}}

